"Both pundits agree Netherlands win, differing only on whether Japan score. NED Pundit predicts a clean 2-0 reflecting the twin absences of Endo and Mitoma as structurally game-changing. JPN Pundit accepts defeat but argues 2-1 — contending Kubo's creativity and Japan's pressing system keep them competitive. Key agreement: De Jong's midfield superiority and the devastating impact of losing both the defensive shield (Endo) and the primary wide threat (Mitoma)."